# Engineering Delivery Standard

- Keep production modules focused. Extract dedicated modules, services, hooks, and components instead of growing route handlers or screen components indefinitely.
- Put automated tests in dedicated test files or test modules. Do not mix extensive test scenarios into production source files.
- Implement the feature first, add or update automated tests, then run the relevant checks before calling it complete.
- Record completed work and verification evidence in the project plan or test report before committing or pushing.
- Do not commit generated artifacts, local models, credentials, uploads, build output, or temporary files.
- Keep user-facing strings in the localization layer and preserve authorization, audit, and data-scope checks when refactoring.
